## Read Trimming and Post-Trimming Quality Control

Adapter and read trimming was performed using Cutadapt on the single-end RNA-seq reads.

Following trimming, FastQC was performed again to assess the quality of the processed reads and evaluate the effectiveness of the preprocessing step.

The post-trimming dataset contained approximately 3.1 million reads, with an average GC content of approximately 50%.

### Post-Trimming Quality Assessment

The post-trimming FastQC analysis showed:

- Good per-base sequence quality
- Good per-sequence quality scores
- Low N content
- No overrepresented sequences
- Reduced adapter signal compared with the raw dataset
- Some warnings remained for sequence composition and duplication-related metrics
- Residual adapter-content signal was still detected

Overall, the processed reads showed acceptable quality for proceeding to downstream RNA-seq analysis.

